Electromagnetics Volume 1 — Steven W. Ellingson (@em-ellingson1: 0, is #reference, #part-of @em-sources) { r_30KS80JAJY91W0FGZMASQW9DJA
Steven W. Ellingson. Electromagnetics, Volume 1, Virginia Tech Publishing, 2018. DOI 10.21061/electromagnetics-vol-1. [Institutional book record](https://vtechworks.lib.vt.edu/handle/10919/84164) · [Screen-reader-friendly book](https://vtechworks.lib.vt.edu/bitstreams/d275ff31-6bf9-48a8-8145-14cd9197f853/download).

Read all nine chapters and work the exercises: preliminary concepts, electric/magnetic fields, transmission lines, vector analysis, electrostatics, steady current, magnetostatics, time-varying fields and plane waves in lossless media. Return to each complete chapter as the learning sequence reaches it.

